# Workflow

This project uses **`AGENTS.md`** (in the repository root) as the single
source of truth for all AI agents. Read it in full before doing any work.

Also read:

- `.workflow/stack.yml` — technology stack
- `.workflow/architecture.yml` — architecture, layers, dependency rules
- `.workflow/conventions.yml` — code style, naming, tests, commits
- `.workflow/workflow.yml` — rules for how the agent works
- `.workflow/presets.yml` — workflow preset (fast / medium / full / custom)
  and the registry of customizable process features

## Blocking

If the required fields (see `workflow.yml → blocking.required_non_empty_fields`)
are not filled in — **do not start work**. Run the *Bootstrap* procedure
from `.workflow/bootstrap.md`: analyze the project, fill out YAML
drafts, get user confirmation.

## Task cycle

The required stages for this project depend on the active preset in
`presets.yml → meta.active_preset`. Respect the flags in `workflow.yml`:
only stages whose feature is enabled are mandatory.

Typical full cycle: **Analyze → Options (≥2, with pros/cons) →
Plan (self-contained, in `.workflow/history/`) → Execute → Verify**.

If `workflow.yml → process.light_tdd.enabled: true`, apply light TDD for
non-trivial behavior changes. Default mode is `strict-lite`: add or update a
focused test first unless there is a clear, explicitly stated reason not to.

If `workflow.yml → process.granular_commits` is enabled and the task is large,
the plan must include a checkpoint checklist in `.workflow/history/`. After
each verified checkpoint, create a commit automatically or ask first,
depending on `process.granular_commits.mode`.

Details are in section 3 of `AGENTS.md`.

## History

- `.workflow/history/YYYY-MM-DD-<slug>.md` per task (analysis / options / plan / checkpoint checklist / result).
- `.workflow/history/events.jsonl` — a structured event log.

## Scope

Don't do unrequested refactors, don't add dependencies without
discussion, and perform destructive actions only with explicit
confirmation.
